{"name":"Ruins of Metal","hex":"#9b8b84","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ruins","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of ruin"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of ruin"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruins"},{"term":"metal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Chemical elements or alloys, their ores, and the mines where their ores come from.\n Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity.\n\n Any material with similar physical properties as those chemical elements, especially as a combination of several of them, such as an alloy.\n\n An element which was not directly created after the Big Bang but instead formed through nuclear reactions; any element other than hydrogen and helium.\n\n Crushed rock, stones etc. used to make a road.\n\n The ore from which a metal is derived.\n A mine from which ores are taken.","Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by strong drum-beats and distorted guitars. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Having the emotional or social characteristics associated with metal music; brash, bold, frank, unyielding, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ruins","blocks":[{"text":"Ruins are the remains of a civilization's architecture. The term refers to formerly intact structures that have fallen into a state of partial or total disrepair over time due to a variety of factors, such as lack of maintenance, deliberate destruction by humans, or uncontrollable destruction by natural phenomena. The most common root causes that yield ruins in their wake are natural disasters, armed conflict, and population decline, with many structures becoming progressively derelict over time due to long-term weathering and scavenging."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Gymnasion_und_Therme_aus_S%C3%BCdwest.jpg/330px-Gymnasion_und_Therme_aus_S%C3%BCdwest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruins"},{"title":"Metal","blocks":[{"text":"A metal is a material that, when polished or fractured, shows a lustrous appearance, and conducts electricity and heat relatively well. These properties are all associated with having electrons available at the Fermi level, as opposed to nonmetallic materials which do not. Metals are typically ductile and malleable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Surb_Amenaprkitch.jpeg/500px-Surb_Amenaprkitch.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Surb_Amenaprkitch.jpeg/500px-Surb_Amenaprkitch.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Holy Saviour's Church in Gyumri after the 1988 Armenian earthquake, the strongest earthquake in the USSR in terms of the number of victims","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASurb_Amenaprkitch.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Post-and-Grant-Avenue-Look.jpg/500px-Post-and-Grant-Avenue-Look.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Post-and-Grant-Avenue-Look.jpg/12